/*
Implement a blocking delay loop that counts down from an integer n to 0.
The loop must not be optimized away by the compiler.

Return the final value of the counter.

This mimics bare-metal delay routines used when hardware timers are unavailable.

Input: An integer n.
Output: 0 after the delay completes.

Constraints:
- Use a busy-wait loop.
- Ensure the loop variable is not optimized away.
- No library delay functions.
*/

int delay_loop(int n){
  volatile counter = n;
  while(counter){
    counter--;
  }
  return counter;
}
